{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-6","title":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.md","line":157,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex#rem:dc-ch6-2-6","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex","label":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6","line":347,"source":"\\begin{remark}[Gauss formula for a hypersurface]\n  \\label{rem:dc-ch6-2-6}\n\n  \\uses{thm:dc-ch6-2-5, def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:2.6}\n  In the case of a hypersurface $f:M^n\\to\\overline{M}^{n+1}$, let $p\\in M$,\n  $\\eta\\in(T_pM)^\\perp$, $|\\eta|=1$, and $\\{e_1,\\dots,e_n\\}$ an orthonormal basis of $T_pM$ in\n  which $S_\\eta=S$ is diagonal, $S(e_i)=\\lambda_ie_i$. Then $H(e_i,e_i)=\\lambda_i$\n  and $H(e_i,e_j)=0$ if $i\\neq j$, so (1) becomes\n  $$\n  K(e_i,e_j)-\\overline{K}(e_i,e_j)=\\lambda_i\\lambda_j.\\qquad(4)\n  $$\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[Gauss formula for a hypersurface] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a64632d6368362d322d36\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23thm%3Adc-ch6-2-5\">↗ thm:dc-ch6-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23def%3Adc-ch6-2-4-principal\">↗ def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:2.6</span></span>In the case of a hypersurface <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:M^n\\to \\overline{M}^{n+1}$\">$f:M^n\\to \\overline{M}^{n+1}$</span>, let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\eta \\in (T_pM)^\\perp $\">$\\eta \\in (T_pM)^\\perp $</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\eta |=1$\">$|\\eta |=1$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ e_1,\\dots ,e_n\\} $\">$\\{ e_1,\\dots ,e_n\\} $</span> an orthonormal basis of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span> in which <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S_\\eta =S$\">$S_\\eta =S$</span> is diagonal, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S(e_i)=\\lambda _ie_i$\">$S(e_i)=\\lambda _ie_i$</span>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H(e_i,e_i)=\\lambda _i$\">$H(e_i,e_i)=\\lambda _i$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H(e_i,e_j)=0$\">$H(e_i,e_j)=0$</span> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$i\\neq j$\">$i\\neq j$</span>, so (1) becomes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  K(e_i,e_j)-\\overline{K}(e_i,e_j)=\\lambda _i\\lambda _j.\\qquad (4)  \\]\">\\[  K(e_i,e_j)-\\overline{K}(e_i,e_j)=\\lambda _i\\lambda _j.\\qquad (4)  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-7-koszul","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5","title":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5","label":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-7","title":"rem:dc-ch6-2-7","label":"rem:dc-ch6-2-7"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex:dc-ch6-2-8","title":"ex:dc-ch6-2-8","label":"ex:dc-ch6-2-8"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#rem:dc-ch6-2-6","title":"rem:dc-ch6-2-6","tex":"\\begin{remark}[Gauss formula for a hypersurface]\n  \\label{rem:dc-ch6-2-6}\n\n  \\uses{thm:dc-ch6-2-5, def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:2.6}\n  In the case of a hypersurface $f:M^n\\to\\overline{M}^{n+1}$, let $p\\in M$,\n  $\\eta\\in(T_pM)^\\perp$, $|\\eta|=1$, and $\\{e_1,\\dots,e_n\\}$ an orthonormal basis of $T_pM$ in\n  which $S_\\eta=S$ is diagonal, $S(e_i)=\\lambda_ie_i$. Then $H(e_i,e_i)=\\lambda_i$\n  and $H(e_i,e_j)=0$ if $i\\neq j$, so (1) becomes\n  $$\n  K(e_i,e_j)-\\overline{K}(e_i,e_j)=\\lambda_i\\lambda_j.\\qquad(4)\n  $$\n\\end{remark}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#thm:dc-ch6-2-5","title":"thm:dc-ch6-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}